{:event/type :flagship-rollout/iteration, :event/iteration 9, :event/repo "kotoba-lang/industry (registry.edn item6 for 13 repos) + cloud-itonami-isic-5520, cloud-itonami-isic-6910 (item2+4 closed)", :event/checklist-stage 6, :event/stage-name "discovery-catalog-demo-field-plus-2-new-template-closures", :event/action "Part 1 (priority): closed checklist item 6 (discovery catalog :demo entry) for the 13 repos already closed on items 2+4 across iterations 4/6/7/8 -- isic-2910, isic-851, isic-6820, isic-0230, isic-2818, isic-6491, isic-9522, isic-0510, isic-1622, isic-3220, isic-4661, isic-750, isic-9200. Worked in a fresh `gh repo clone kotoba-lang/industry` (never the shared orgs/ checkout), correlating each repo to its registry.edn entry on BOTH :business-id and :repo per the known upstream mismatch (ledger seq 5). This fresh clone's tip (0158ab2c, 2026-07-18T08:45:41Z) was newer than the shared checkout's stale west.yml pin (e3e78c49) -- re-verifying against the fresh clone caught a real false negative: an initial check against the shared (stale) checkout showed isic-4661 with ZERO registry.edn entry at all, but the fresh clone showed a real entry existed (added between the stale pin and now) -- another instance of the checkout-lag class of bug this rollout has repeatedly documented (seq 5, seq 7), this time affecting registry lookups, not just west.yml. SEPARATELY DISCOVERED, not assumed: 12 of the 13 repos already had a :demo field, added by an entirely unrelated, pre-Wave5 bulk-default commit (kotoba-lang/industry commit 2d7b46db9, 'registry: default github.io demos for all numeric ISIC entries', 2026-07-17, one day before ADR-2607189300 even existed) that mechanically set :demo to each repo's BARE GitHub Pages root for every numeric ISIC entry, regardless of whether that root actually served anything demo-related. Verified live (curl) that these bare-root URLs serve a DIFFERENT, hand-authored marketing/blueprint page, not the real build-time-generated demo -- concretely, isic-6491's bare root literally titles itself 'Financial leasing — Open Business Blueprint (ISIC 6491)', and isic-2910's root titles itself 'Manufacture of Motor Vehicles | cloud-itonami-isic-2910' vs. the real generated demo's distinct title 'cloud-itonami-isic-2910 · motor-vehicle plant'. Corrected all 13 (12 updated from the wrong bare-root default, 1 added for isic-6491 which had no :demo field at all) to point at the verified real artifact instead: https://cloud-itonami.github.io/cloud-itonami-<repo>/samples/operator-console.html. Part 2 (time/budget allowed after Part 1 landed cleanly): extended the item2+4 template (proven across 13 uses in iterations 4/6/7/8) to 2 more diverse-sector repos, reusing 2 pre-vetted backup candidates iteration 8 explicitly flagged but did not use -- cloud-itonami-isic-5520 (camping grounds / RV parks / trailer parks, campgroundops) and cloud-itonami-isic-6910 (business formation / company registration agent, formation) -- dispatched as 2 independent, fully self-contained background agents (no shared context) with the complete proven pipeline brief (mine real seed data from the repo's own store/governor/operation.cljc, verify sim.cljc against real seed data before trusting it per the isic-851 trap restated verbatim, build a genuine multi-disposition scenario, idempotency via sha256 x2 + CI-layout simulation, run tests, verify pure forward progress via gh api compare before merging, server-side merge, real workflow_dispatch polled to completion, live Pages curl).", :event/verification "Part 1: fresh-cloned all 13 registry-entry edits, validated the edn still parses (clojure.edn/read-string) and that entry count (650) and id set are byte-for-byte unchanged before/after -- only the 13 :demo field values changed (confirmed via before/after grep diff of every :demo occurrence in the file, showing exactly 13 lines differ, no other entry touched). Independently re-verified all 13 live demo URLs FRESH from GitHub Pages (not local disk, not trusting prior iterations' ledger claims) before writing anything: curl -sSL -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' against https://cloud-itonami.github.io/cloud-itonami-<repo>/samples/operator-console.html for all 13 returned HTTP 200 with distinct, real, sector-specific <title> tags and non-trivial page sizes (4.8KB-7.5KB), zero occurrences of '404' in any response body. Pushed branch flagship-wave5-item6-demo-fields-13repos to kotoba-lang/industry, verified pure forward progress via gh api compare (ahead_by 1, behind_by 0, merge_base == old main tip) before merging, server-side merged via gh api repos/kotoba-lang/industry/merges (commit f6cd5622e5423a34eb778c8bb7e215cfb9979069), deleted the remote branch. Re-fetched the MERGED file directly from GitHub's contents API afterward (not a self-report) and re-parsed it, confirming all 13 :demo fields equal exactly 'https://cloud-itonami.github.io/cloud-itonami-isic-<N>/samples/operator-console.html' for their respective repos. Advanced manifest/west.yml's industry pin (e3e78c49 -> f6cd5622) via the mandated single-entry sha-guarded GitHub API PUT (commit a814dcd2b2d9b115c8fa2b88d3184394db5baa3d on com-junkawasaki/root main), first verifying pure forward progress via gh api compare (ahead_by 263, behind_by 0, merge_base == old pin). Synced the shared superproject main checkout to origin (repairing a shallow-graft '(forced update)'/'unrelated histories' false positive via gh api compare confirming pure fast-forward, then git fetch --deepen=15 + git merge --ff-only per CLAUDE.md's documented remedy) and ran `west update --fetch smart industry` to bring the shared orgs/kotoba-lang/industry checkout to zero lag -- confirmed via git -C orgs/kotoba-lang/industry rev-parse HEAD == f6cd5622. Part 2: both agents' results independently re-verified centrally (not trusted at face value) -- gh api repos/cloud-itonami/<repo>/commits/main confirmed each reported merge SHA is exactly the current main tip (isic-5520: d24153ed8b3d29